# Environment files (contain secrets)
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
# Timestamped/ad-hoc .env BACKUPS. A bare `.env` pattern does NOT match
# `.env.bak-ollama-084227` and friends, so a backup taken while switching
# providers sat untracked-but-committable carrying the REAL SECRET_KEY,
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY, MISTRAL_API_KEY, LANGSMITH_API_KEY
# and DATABASE_URL. One `git add -A` would have published live credentials.
.env.bak*
*.env.bak*
.env.backup*
# Local-dev compose env (devs copy from app.env.example).
# The .example template IS committed; the real file is not.
/app.env
# Template env files (committed .example variants are exceptions to .env ignore)
/env-templates/.env.*
!/env-templates/.env.*.example

# Local-dev compose overrides — see app.env.example for the convention.
docker-compose.override.yml

# ── Terraform state and key material, REPO-WIDE (F-28) ───────────────────────
# `infra/.gitignore` already carries the full Terraform guardrail set for
# `infra/**`, including the `!terraform/{app,foundation}/<env>.tfvars` and
# `!terraform/**/localstack.tfvars` exceptions that keep the seven committed,
# non-secret per-environment config files tracked. It remains the AUTHORITY for
# that subtree — a nested .gitignore takes precedence, so a negation there
# cannot be overridden from here, and duplicating its exception list in this
# file would only create a second copy to drift.
#
# What was missing is coverage OUTSIDE `infra/`. A `terraform.tfstate` written
# at the repo root, a `.pem` dropped in `backend/`, or a `secrets.tfvars` under
# `scripts/` matched nothing at all. Nothing has leaked — gitleaks scans full
# history on every CI run — but "no detector happened to match" is not the same
# as "it could not be committed", and a state file is plaintext by design.
#
# `.terraform.lock.hcl` is deliberately NOT matched: it pins provider versions
# and is committed on purpose.
*.tfvars
*.tfvars.json
*.auto.tfvars
*.auto.tfvars.json
!*.tfvars.example
*.tfstate
*.tfstate.*
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.*
.terraform/
.terraformrc
terraform.rc
crash.log
crash.*.log
override.tf
override.tf.json
*_override.tf
*_override.tf.json

# Private keys, certificate bundles and keystores. No file with any of these
# extensions is tracked today; these patterns keep it that way.
*.pem
*.key
*.pfx
*.p12
*.jks
*.keystore

